# .dropboxignore  (repo-backend-v2)
#
# Project-scoped additions on top of workspace/.dropboxignore, which already
# covers node_modules, logs, tmp, coverage, .DS_Store and .idea for every
# project under the workspace folder. Only put rules here that should NOT
# apply workspace-wide.
#
# Patterns are matched relative to this file's folder.

# ---- Live credentials: keep local, never replicate to a third party --------
# .env holds production secrets for services this app talks to: TOKEN_SECRET,
# ARCHIVESPACE_PASSWORD, DURACLOUD_PWD, ARCHIVEMATICA_API_KEY,
# ARCHIVEMATICA_STORAGE_API_KEY, TN_SERVICE_API_KEY, CONVERT_SERVICE_API_KEY,
# HANDLE_API_KEY, CURATION_API_KEY and the DB credentials. Git already ignores
# it; this stops Dropbox from syncing it as well.
#
# WARNING — this is not like node_modules: .env is NOT regenerable. Once
# Dropbox applies this rule the file is removed from the cloud and from your
# OTHER devices, and survives only on machines that already hold a copy.
# Before adding a new machine, copy .env there out-of-band (or rebuild it from
# .env-example plus the secret store) — it will not arrive via sync.
.env
